4. Operations: Retrofitting Existing ASR Replicas

To immediately realize the FinOps savings on existing protected VMs, the passive Premium SSD replica disks must be downgraded to Standard HDD. Because Azure Site Recovery maintains a continuous Shared Access Signature (SAS) lock on these disks to write replication data, the disk SKU cannot be modified directly.

The following procedure safely removes the lock, changes the tier, and allows ASR to automatically self-heal and resume replication.

4.1. The Direct Method (Cancel Export)

In the Azure Portal, navigate to the Target DR Resource Group and select the passive replica disk resource.

In the left-hand menu, under Settings, select Disk Export.

Click the Cancel export button.

Mechanism: This destroys the active SAS token, instantly unlocking the disk for modifications.

[Screen: The Disk Export page with a red box highlighting the "Cancel export" button]

Wait 1 to 2 minutes, then strictly refresh the browser (Ctrl + F5).

On the disk's Overview page, verify that the Disk state has changed from Active SAS to Unattached.

[Screen: The disk Overview page highlighting the "Disk state" field reading "Unattached"]

In the left-hand menu, select Size + performance.

Change the storage SKU from Premium SSD to Standard HDD, then click Save.

[Screen: The "Size + performance" blade showing Standard HDD selected and the Save button highlighted]

Auto-Recovery: No further action is required. Within 15 to 30 minutes, ASR will automatically detect the missing lock, request a new SAS token, and resume delta replication. (Temporary Warning or Critical states in the Recovery Vault during this window are expected and normal).

4.2. The Fallback Method (Pause Replication)
If ASR's aggressive background processes immediately recreate the SAS lock before you can save the new SKU, use this fallback method to temporarily halt the replication engine.

Navigate to the Recovery Services Vault, go to Replicated items, and select the target VM.

At the top of the overview page, click Pause Replication.

[Screen: The Replicated item overview page with a red box around the "Pause Replication" button]

Return to the replica disk resource. If it is not already unlocked, repeat the "Cancel export" step above.

Navigate to Size + performance and change the SKU to Standard HDD.

Return to the Replicated item in the Recovery Services Vault and click Resume Replication.

[Screen: The Replicated item overview page showing the "Resume Replication" button]
